# With-draft profile for a unified-memory host (the aarch64 / GB10-class box in README >
# Cards tested on). Same sizing as with-draft.env; the difference is GPU_SPLIT.
#
#   PROFILE=spark-with-draft bash serve.sh
#
# GPU_SPLIT is what raises the load budget on a unified-memory box. Leave it unset and model.py
# applies its 0.5 GB reserve default, freezing the process at (mem_get_info free - 0.5) / total -
# and CUDA's free excludes the reclaimable page cache that is holding the pack, so that reads as a
# fraction of the memory the box actually has. serve.sh evicts the cache before launch, which is
# necessary but not sufficient: the budget also has to cover the loader's own measuring transient.
#
# 112 is measured on a 121.7 GiB box, not chosen. The measuring forward records a ~983 MiB
# transient at layer 39 and refuses a budget with less than 983 + 256 MiB of headroom:
# GPU_SPLIT=119 dies at layer 39 with 1220 MiB free where 1239 MiB is required, and 112 loads with
# ~112 GiB reported free.
CTX=65536
CACHE_SIZE=65536
AUTOSPLIT_MAX_BATCH=16
MAX_ACTIVE_REQUESTS=16
MAX_PENDING_REQUESTS=64
DRAFT=1
GPU_SPLIT=112
